      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The organizational strategy used in a high risk Coronary Angioplasty procedure is discussed. The attempted vessel was a severely stenosed Right Coronary Artery in a patient who had undergone triple graft, with residual obstruction of Left Main Artery and only one patent venous graft on a marginal branch of the Circumflex artery. The procedure was performed using a Stack type autoperfusion balloon angioplasty catheter, with a Cardiopulmonary Support System held in standby."},
